</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"9af55ccb1fba" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-1.4Namingconvent=
ions">1.4 Naming conventions</h2>
<p local-id=3D"c3a1e1d5780d">I.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; F=
olders should always use snake_case</p>
<p local-id=3D"0a2a3083f303">II.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Python files=
 should always use snake_case</p>
<p local-id=3D"67d5ac0c087b">III.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Azure devops projects s=
hould use PascalCase</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"05deb95047f9" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-1.5Filesize">1.5=
&nbsp;File size</h2>
<p local-id=3D"bec967fd8a05">Try to keep files smaller than 500 lines of co=
de. If necessary, split the file into multiple, following code design princ=
iples.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0a5a8bd17f03">&nbsp;</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"0fb4d7e4803f" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.CodeDesign">2.=
&nbsp; Code Design</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"6a1f1dd41df5" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.1Pattern">2.1&=
nbsp; Pattern</h2>
<p local-id=3D"ccd8418c758c">The design pattern that will be used, is the C=
ontroller =E2=80=93 Service =E2=80=93 Repository (CSR) pattern, which is fu=
rther explained in the in-depth Design document.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"8e=
d1b7b0-3650-4334-adb8-6452d9b74ed2" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c6b8f87a-f0d7-486a-9d39-4f8d930d5a2e">
<td data-local-id=3D"664c5710-65fa-4713-a9da-78b56a0aada8" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0e3d644d7e33"><strong>Type</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c31b017a-1940-4dc8-90bb-2d42384bafd0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c9f97afeb4a3"><strong>Usage</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"b7848621-a612-4b6f-b75b-a3049d3323ec">
<td data-local-id=3D"5fe8092e-4fba-4eea-8f8d-8dfad25eb591" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"da4c36394dca">Controller</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"69379b69-b068-409f-b4b4-e45587861e3d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"aff9a71f027e">Handles and orchestrates processing of (user) =
data. Includes light validation, but not business logic validation. Topmost=
 layer for handling processing errors</p>
<p local-id=3D"e3f45a73ce7c">Must NOT contain business logic</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"4f09b771-f408-4c5d-8d91-67b19dd6fd65">
<td data-local-id=3D"678cf220-d8e6-4b7d-9b1e-f1773f558b7d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"45fb6e36fab8">Service</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"36ec4620-719b-48d7-aa20-c4e3a41735aa" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d4917225f2ce">Business logic such as calculations, transform=
ations, API calls etc. Services should stay small and only have a single pu=
rpose</p>
<p local-id=3D"2b8baedeb775">Must NOT call the database or disk or communic=
ate with its external user</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"6a80d4fa-8854-4392-b980-3cca2d4c81cb">
<td data-local-id=3D"8388ea92-b068-4627-b4f5-547c58283be7" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7c0698f2e81e">Repository</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"631a2e7e-b5b0-433d-b0d3-92247fb5a2eb" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"2334f6f88915">Used for reading and writing files and operati=
ons that involve the database. Can handle API calls too if they regard stor=
ing/retrieving data</p>
<p local-id=3D"4ec9fcc8907a">Must NOT contain business logic</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"5a8e603b-acd1-4b00-b556-df0ecd0cf6e1">
<td data-local-id=3D"6973246a-f2bc-4eda-9d20-81d1ba589420" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b6a25ed43452">Factory</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"93a7cf9a-ea1d-4c2a-8726-c51a7b115084" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"39aa1f4b3dc3">Helper class that can instantiate classes with=
 a single function. Usually, a factory exists per CSR. Use whenever class i=
nstantiation becomes frequent and requires more and more dependencies.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"a833a2722a6d" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.2Classes">2.2&=
nbsp; Classes</h2>
<p local-id=3D"8ae35573c457">A class should be made when any of the followi=
ng applies:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8a5d328f705e">
<li local-id=3D"3f3dea9b7ee5">
<p local-id=3D"196da0368c92">Code is domain specific as described above</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"6b101301fd51">
<p local-id=3D"d2f6ca2fb3b5">It requires processing of stateful data</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"b60e38f6ad6f">
<p local-id=3D"bdf531013d2c">Functions/operations can be grouped</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7d2394f2cdc0">
<p local-id=3D"646fa4a2038c">Abstraction of a subject (person, object, etc)=
 is required</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"5108f82a961e" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.2.1Dependencie=
s">2.2.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dependencies</h3>
<p local-id=3D"49fd8f4d17c5">To make sure that classes stay testable, depen=
dencies must be injected via the constructor (__init__) of the class where =
possible. In some cases, this will not be possible, such as stateful object=
s.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"9381ed8eaa61" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.2.2Inheritance=
">2.2.2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Inheritance</h3>
<p local-id=3D"27ae9b26207e">Inheritance is allowed but advised against. Ne=
sted inheritance often results in code that is hard to debug and test. It d=
oes work well for enforcing certain patterns when developing generalized pa=
ckages.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"08cdc41b2f4f" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.3Functions">2.=
3&nbsp; Functions</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"ec67fd1be06d">
<li local-id=3D"ef2585a332e8">
<p local-id=3D"6f0a5bfd2b9c">Should only have a single purpose where possib=
le</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cd4047b392c6">
<p local-id=3D"edb845d146b3">Keep functions small and always ask yourself w=
hether it is necessary to have a longer function</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0bd5bcd90469">
<p local-id=3D"e24c85381f1e">When the number of parameters exceeds five, co=
nsider using models or splitting the function into smaller sections</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"4e9a992b8961">
<p local-id=3D"ccca635855a5">Use private functions (prefixed with an unders=
core) that are for internal usage only, for example inside a class</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"0179d7aeab29" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.4Configuration=
">2.4&nbsp; Configuration</h2>
<p local-id=3D"5cffb9beec71">The Azure environments use environment variabl=
es to set static configurations. This needs to be replicated locally:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"b0e6d0806ecb">
<li local-id=3D"a10d50af7928">
<p local-id=3D"d1df6e838c52">Use .env for setting the environment variables=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5dfd779db033">
<p local-id=3D"8b4d29c453be">Make a config.py file where you use Pydantic S=
ettings to make a config class</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da4ec3e9ab86">
<p local-id=3D"a482c1a92fcc">Use the config class for all static configurat=
ion data in your scripts</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"5e69f9bdd25d" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.5Errorhandling=
">2.5&nbsp; Error handling</h2>
<p local-id=3D"96f538e4b0d0">When errors are raised, they need to be propag=
ated properly. Main error handling should be done inside a controller/orche=
strator, since these handle the flow of the data.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"302a91d3f66a">
<li local-id=3D"26432dd65e18">
<p local-id=3D"9ca45f86eb4a">Controller =E2=80=93 receives domain and syste=
m errors from subclasses and handles accordingly. Does the error stop the p=
rocess? Or should we continue?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cff970a028dd">
<p local-id=3D"d4ee9731217a">Service =E2=80=93 Raises domain specific error=
s to indicate a process has failed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8e7d63a07a2e">
<p local-id=3D"beb22ba1d65c">Repository =E2=80=93 Should always raise error=
s that are workable for the service layer. Switching out your datasource fr=
om files to databases should not impact the business logic, therefore you s=
hould catch errors and transform into a workable error format</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"34f9e2261bfe" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-2.6Logging">2.6&=
nbsp; Logging</h2>
<p local-id=3D"af5224e96e45">There are some hard requirements for logs:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c3bf87067287">
<li local-id=3D"f5e7af002f79">
<p local-id=3D"cc7e2bdbe201">Use the logger template</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1612436c8abd">
<p local-id=3D"9e463f9ecfc9">Sensitive information is a hard no</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9836e663d56b">
<p local-id=3D"159e1022cdc0">Must be descriptive: what is going on and why?=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b15e8a1036e">
<p local-id=3D"6e69b37aa0d2">Can include a stacktrace in local and developm=
ent environments, ideally not in production</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3a22d5ac9dcd">
<p local-id=3D"31ba0f65b3e8">Only important information should be logged, n=
o debug texts or&nbsp; =E2=80=9CProcess now on step 2=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"87ee46b337a8">
<p local-id=3D"4bf7984ed630">Use .info for process information such as metr=
ics, confirmations that something has been received, and aborts that are no=
t error related but expected</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a8e066703aaa">
<p local-id=3D"44ba9309ec2a">Use .warning for intended behavior that was no=
t supposed to happen, but also not critical enough to stop the application.=
 Think of functions/endpoints that are deprecated, or no files coming in du=
ring daily processing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"275a4b7e4bbe">
<p local-id=3D"a429f0fde024">Use .error for anything that needs to be resol=
ved directly, and which are critical for the application. Error will trigge=
r a notification to the team</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"48e646b33f29"></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"c4217106d2be" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.CodeStyle">3.&=
nbsp; Code Style&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"027806b2ccba" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.1Generalprinci=
ples">3.1&nbsp; General principles</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"9cc4ffe182bc">
<li local-id=3D"006afee29c47">
<p local-id=3D"512bae440111">Follow PEP8</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8352f5171b1c">
<p local-id=3D"e246e66cf865">Make code easy to read, not complex &amp; clev=
er</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c812b8c648e5">
<p local-id=3D"ebe2ff222d71">Consistency over preferences</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fe1747fd4893">
<p local-id=3D"ec522b5a2eb0">Explicit over implicit</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"2bdaa0cc8ccb" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.2Formatting">3=
.2&nbsp; Formatting</h2>
<p local-id=3D"cc1f7490f1cc">Formatting is standardized via tooling. For fo=
rmatting, please use Black on the default settings. You can download Black =
via the Visual Studio Code extension store, or via pip. Use black after eac=
h safe or before each commit! Developers should not mess around with the se=
ttings or formatting themselves.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"070db5ae226b" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.3Linting">3.3&=
nbsp; Linting</h2>
<p local-id=3D"2a8606264881">SonarQube for IDE is the main linting tool and=
 is available via the Visual Studio Code extension store.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"85f71ebef043" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.4Namingconvent=
ions">3.4&nbsp; Naming conventions</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"eb=
a6556a-0e1a-4668-a6b2-78e7443c983f" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"8cd0435b-7fed-4585-94d2-5e477c26675a">
<td data-local-id=3D"a6e48f58-12cc-483f-9b40-66b9a19c39c6" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"78f1ca2bc57d"><strong>Situation</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"0eccc209-cff0-484f-8999-35cf9d154036" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e51f64e560f9"><strong>What to use?</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"fcfbc18c-312b-44ee-9348-89a7c1ea3ea0">
<td data-local-id=3D"75986c45-1966-44e3-a067-f4fd931fab2d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"84428e0137e4">General</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"380c56c4-366f-44b5-9fd4-ebea5ab0eca3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"fae830590212">
<li local-id=3D"3407dd39d808">
<p local-id=3D"6a14405b9140">Underscore for internal (private) functionalit=
y</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3668cd8c57f7">
<p local-id=3D"174164aa43a2">Explicit and descriptive naming</p></li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"9ca53a06-dc97-4555-9dba-1ffcbafb8070">
<td data-local-id=3D"b6262c5d-2194-4a04-9a8d-e26ab9884ee4" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a968cacb19a4">Variables</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"68ad0226-82b1-40f0-a176-7cc74920ae67" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"8693f9b8987e">
<li local-id=3D"0e3f0a20bffe">
<p local-id=3D"3389526b3ebb">snake_case</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a317d00a7792">
<p local-id=3D"2705c15d28e5">Can be short for mathematical formulas</p></li=
>
</ul></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"6aeb1db7-37d4-4481-b20d-9e7dd1f45db6">
<td data-local-id=3D"1f084fa1-2ba2-4455-9192-0ff7b4e43530" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"67acfc941505">Functions</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"babd0068-c8f4-449e-9110-904cb67ed86e" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"55d214d38deb">
<li local-id=3D"6de3013660c1">
<p local-id=3D"da9c6ffcac5f">snake_case</p></li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f2ac6719-d56d-40d4-b7ad-d49511f2d47b">
<td data-local-id=3D"f36573fd-6090-404f-8131-971f3f1a7625" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5b76f5fdbd57">Constants</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c99ebb25-aba4-47d7-8a46-627b1efab8b7" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"18098b5bd8fc">
<li local-id=3D"b33866cd92a7">
<p local-id=3D"70e927430fd2">UPPER_SNAKE_CASE</p></li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"31faa273-5bb1-47f8-85e6-035d79979d0e">
<td data-local-id=3D"ce51d103-e907-4b5d-8cdd-f213c739bfa2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5b133defd6c1">Classes</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a542aa0f-ee4e-43ed-b43e-91c7d43aa414" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"404a57270a97">
<li local-id=3D"187bb0bb0764">
<p local-id=3D"df9edc94b9ea">PascalCase</p></li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"16e75415-4241-4162-abb3-b9bc06f5674f">
<td data-local-id=3D"c4696911-5961-433c-84fb-3df310c3867f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"473c3e78547d">Booleans</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"7be47fd0-ac15-456d-89cf-2605599b712b" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<ul local-id=3D"f0775cdab282">
<li local-id=3D"34267df0ded5">
<p local-id=3D"243337ce86e2">Prefix with is_, has_ or should_</p></li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"da8c6e987781" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.5Imports">3.5&=
nbsp; Imports</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"f9bb6f90167e">
<li local-id=3D"a446960a22f5">
<p local-id=3D"174ae9010263">Only used imports</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9accd01a1309">
<p local-id=3D"1fc414c45338">Preferably no wildcards (*) as this might clas=
h with other imports</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7fed140652c">
<p local-id=3D"9b4882126ea8">Preferably use =E2=80=9Cfrom &lt;module&gt; im=
port &lt;item&gt;=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"12154ca0570c">
<p local-id=3D"1aff65b26db0">Alphabetical order per group, whitespace betwe=
en groups</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f3a775d0714f">
<p local-id=3D"167fc5fd952a">Grouped into:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c3a106fbb392">
<li local-id=3D"2ce13f562319">
<p local-id=3D"c9f7f00214c5">Python native packages</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"17c1593ab573">
<p local-id=3D"bc57e0a4ad79">External packages</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9d0d0aa753ab">
<p local-id=3D"2eceba391843">Own modules</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"b95e726aff1c" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-3.6Readability">=
3.6&nbsp; Readability</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"9286246a4ae3">
<li local-id=3D"f61a4b746c0a">
<p local-id=3D"7688c6ff7990">Avoid long and complex code</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2a2166c92416">
<li local-id=3D"b6391454c3c7">
<p local-id=3D"480d265e3b08">Split long lines into steps</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"22fe0568960e">
<p local-id=3D"a4bb99d81de6">Split long functions into smaller functions</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"4fa4a2ab6118">
<p local-id=3D"5aeb488b9726">Prefer being explicit over implicit</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e07b18309d7d">
<p local-id=3D"5e0784906383">If explicit names become too long, the functio=
n/class is doing too much</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"cdf6c39a2497">
<p local-id=3D"41d9c6ec503a">Describe with comments what is happening and w=
hy decisions were made if the code itself is not clear enough. Think of the=
 usage of certain constants</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c5bf3de72a00">
<p local-id=3D"78fdaa86cddc">Don=E2=80=99t use code that is super nested, s=
uch as multiple loops inside loops, or classes that inherits from a class t=
hat also inherits from a class</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23c6fda61fbf">
<p local-id=3D"64694ef51781">Use type hints where applicable</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"01f8881e83be"></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"4133ad243e93" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.Documentation"=
>4.&nbsp; Documentation</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"124ed3b2bfc4" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.1Project">4.1&=
nbsp; Project</h2>
<p local-id=3D"13564489b1a8">Each project is expected to have documentation=
 available on Confluence. Depending on the size and the goal of the project=
, sometimes a RSDP is required. Please give a general description of:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"304ac108c432">
<li local-id=3D"09f97a7cdb50">
<p local-id=3D"906c90aa4891">Why was this project started?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"346e8a7b1441">
<p local-id=3D"30490eaf73fb">Who is the owner?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ade07c75de67">
<p local-id=3D"d23290bf0720">Who is the maintainer?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"11204bcb8f8e">
<p local-id=3D"074f04f70d19">How can we set it up ourselves?</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"567946882f0e">
<p local-id=3D"eb91a85d34d9">Are there rules for contributors?</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"f1f0abd9725d" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.2Repository">4=
.2&nbsp; Repository</h2>
<p local-id=3D"3cee1ff19df3">A repository should be able to function by its=
elf; therefore, it requires a README.md file that explains how to set it up=
 and run it. Add:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"df73c5e9afa3">
<li local-id=3D"00515cb95acc">
<p local-id=3D"9a6a87d7f5b2">Intended functionality</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c70e83f3b7d">
<p local-id=3D"ecd05df5b230">Env variables</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ccf6a43098b7">
<p local-id=3D"2659e3915132">How to set up</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"e2ee36d1d5c9" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.3Code">4.3&nbs=
p; Code</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"7364b4c3d451" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.3.1Docstrings"=
>4.3.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Docstrings</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0e48fa1757ca">For docstrings, please use AutoDocstring on th=
e default settings. This extension is available via the Visual Studio Code =
extension store. Docstring should contain:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d3c8dd489827">
<li local-id=3D"43bd97208042">
<p local-id=3D"a2a246c70a7f">Short one-liner what the function does</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"e3d9c332c28f">
<p local-id=3D"e1af0f089c20">The input and output types and what they mean<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa5150ea8c73">
<p local-id=3D"19fd0859f377">Incase of public usage (such as packages), als=
o provide additional notes and usage guide</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"2f77ca464a49">For private functions only a short description=
 is required. No need for input and output type explanations.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"ad40067a95ef" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.3.2Typehints">=
4.3.2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Type hints</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a2c8a33f6abc">Though debatable, type hints are an important =
part of documenting your code. Use type hints for all function inputs and o=
utputs, and class attributes, with an exception for:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"36d293147941">
<li local-id=3D"21085967e7a6">
<p local-id=3D"88da88fa1403">self or cls for classes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7f9fd41f7929">
<p local-id=3D"707d5e914cbb">The output type for __init__, which is always =
None</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ef44f8212d84">As of Python 3.10, you can use Python native t=
ypes for type hinting. No need to import List from the typing library, just=
 use list. Usage of complex type hinting, such as annotations and custom ty=
pes, is encouraged.</p>
<p local-id=3D"afb2d03f604e">For static type checking, we are using MyPy Ty=
pe Checker, an extension in the Visual Studio Code extension store.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"d8aa1f0aceda" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-4.3.3Inlinecomme=
nts">4.3.3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Inline comments</h3>
<p local-id=3D"301b2fffd9f2">Use inline comments to describe what is going =
on and why. It is not necessary to do this for each line of code, as it is =
expected that your code is descriptive and logical enough to understand on =
the spot. However, in a lot of cases, it is not directly clear why certain =
choices are made. Make comments for:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"19f96b2cb36d">
<li local-id=3D"d158085d9fc4">
<p local-id=3D"77d6a27c2b4e">Magic numbers such as multipliers to indicate =
why that number was chosen</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a763088aa9fa">
<p local-id=3D"9ccb01332481">Loops and complex decision trees</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5f69f152914b">
<p local-id=3D"79fc5d8d5303">Early escapes/aborts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d72dffc9bb6b">
<p local-id=3D"d8a67fd96479">Etc.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"dcee1c4d4f87"></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"b63add9fce2e" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.VersionControl=
">5.&nbsp; Version Control</h1>
<p local-id=3D"e227c2741187">Following the standards (section 1), you shoul=
d already have a project and a repository in Azure DevOps. For that reason,=
 this section will not talk about setting up your project.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"33b0d3f339ce" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.1Branching">5.=
1&nbsp; Branching</h2>
<p local-id=3D"fa25fa22aa74">When writing new features or fixes, you are re=
quired to branch from the local development branch. &nbsp;</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"2e1c146bc450" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.1.1Namingconve=
ntions">5.1.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Naming conventions</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"54b14a1deb98">
<li local-id=3D"4fa4ea6a6058">
<p local-id=3D"eee0c8097225">New feature -&gt; feat/&lt;description&gt;</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"a51e51a895e9">
<p local-id=3D"0726739f683e">Bugfix -&gt; bugfix/&lt;description&gt;</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"c4ddfb4a1b14">
<p local-id=3D"e5f5393c22aa">Hotfix -&gt; hotfix/&lt;description&gt;</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"3e3bdb350722">
<p local-id=3D"9156ae346285">Documentation -&gt; docs/&lt;description&gt;</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5da6e3b27799">
<p local-id=3D"44bc6197858d">Refactoring -&gt; refactor/&lt;description&gt;=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"39ea126a8ade">
<p local-id=3D"c5432ce8b268">All names should be kebab-case</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3045be751b32">
<p local-id=3D"f8dcef67cbad">Description should be a few words</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cd4fad0ccd9">
<p local-id=3D"294171e2c0c6">In case a ticket is linked, use the ticket ID =
in the description</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"9c217995ff50" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.1.2Branchflow"=
>5.1.2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Branch flow</h3>
<p local-id=3D"f240a99919a6">All repositories should have the following pro=
tected branches by default:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a8faf7fe04e9">
<li local-id=3D"3358be8d2678">
<p local-id=3D"4d0b58d598b0">master/main</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7fdb17ed1795">
<p local-id=3D"506b7b058269">development/dev</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1483e1646e66">
<p local-id=3D"ec036f5cad00">local-development/local-dev</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"88af0386a46e">Making the flow:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b31d0c43cc05">
<li local-id=3D"ff62305e04aa">
<p local-id=3D"3be8e6a4e38d">Branch out from local-development</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b298f271355f">
<p local-id=3D"265911092263">Build and write code</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa807002481c">
<p local-id=3D"65e2fc03cf4b">Pull request from new branch towards local-dev=
elopment</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0e2d2542264d">
<p local-id=3D"f04d99f718ff">Developers test new code</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa412cc4d956">
<p local-id=3D"0bbd8015ab86">Pull request from local-development towards de=
velopment</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2acfe6de4dea">
<p local-id=3D"34a742423f85">Code should be tested on the platform and insi=
de CI/CD pipeline</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"09f3be71e5af">
<p local-id=3D"5d6e338f27bd">Pull request from development towards master</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4388e491bddf">
<p local-id=3D"6ca0060bb01c">Merge after management approval</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"a1da8f82bac3" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.2Commits">5.2&=
nbsp; Commits</h2>
<p local-id=3D"6fa68f7c9a59">For code commits we follow the conventional co=
mmit standard as described in:<br><a class=3D"external-link" data-card-appe=
arance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/" l=
ocal-id=3D"80e627de6aa8" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.conventionalcommits.o=
rg/en/v1.0.0/</a></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"8464a4a109ab" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-5.3Pullrequests"=
>5.3&nbsp; Pull requests</h2>
<p local-id=3D"22ec91b3352d">A few things are required for pull requests:</=
p>
<ul local-id=3D"7476db4a6d67">
<li local-id=3D"46ac309dafef">
<p local-id=3D"bda73111622a">A descriptive title</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"eff1301621a3">
<p local-id=3D"2b40ccfecc36">A description that contains:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"50bfc36f7a4f">
<li local-id=3D"e95f1f15dc53">
<p local-id=3D"b70b8f6d06c2">What has changed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b0776e3a175">
<p local-id=3D"798c1069830e">How to test what is new (if anything new is ad=
ded)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9a974ca06f79">
<p local-id=3D"b42b03823d02">A reference to the ticket if available</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"010c329744bb">
<p local-id=3D"7de665583049">At least two people review code coming into lo=
cal-development, development and master</p>
<ul local-id=3D"11827acd9708">
<li local-id=3D"7c67548c1e27">
<p local-id=3D"90b89ca003ef">One person is familiar with what the code is s=
upposed to do</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8401592423d6">
<p local-id=3D"3801f7b0bf68">One person is familiar with Python</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"ff737d637e88">
<p local-id=3D"f1374571b2c2">Pull requests coming into master should have t=
he code owner and one member of management as additional reviewers. Code sh=
ould not be allowed to merge if no approval from management is given</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"32fa98019d1f">
<p local-id=3D"ad17e7aa8fec">Comments after initial review should be resolv=
ed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e6aeb59ef81">
<p local-id=3D"a31609f562de">Branch should be removed after pull request is=
 merged</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"09da2e43d3df"></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"1b413b556733" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.Misc">6.&nbsp;=
 Misc</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"0512515c9621" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.1Howtostartyou=
rcodingenvironment?">6.1&nbsp; How to start your coding environment?</h2>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"cb6c0ebe9aaa">
<li local-id=3D"908a8483ecd9">
<p local-id=3D"270fa9f20bad">Git clone from the Azure DevOps repository</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"a5a2761cc646">
<p local-id=3D"d5c0da3cf4bb">Construct a new venv running =E2=80=9Cpython -=
m venv venv=E2=80=9D inside the terminal</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"975f502a0db0">
<p local-id=3D"bb2ee299bb25">Open the venv running =E2=80=9Cvenv/Scripts/ac=
tivate=E2=80=9D inside the terminal</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"55c6c2210c50">
<p local-id=3D"7830317d86e2">You can now confirm that the venv is open by c=
hecking the prefix in the terminal. It is supposed to start with =E2=80=9C&=
lt;terminal name&gt;(venv) : &lt;command here&gt;=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7c0792b839fe">
<p local-id=3D"14c9aed02974">In case this is an existing project, run =E2=
=80=9Cpip install -r requirements=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d283b03f660e">
<p local-id=3D"7f6641e31d12">You should now be ready to start your script w=
ith =E2=80=9Cpython main.py=E2=80=9D depending on the project setup</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"2eba5dde7fad">
<p local-id=3D"473bcb49624a">When restarting your computer or Visual Studio=
 Code, restart at 3.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"428acc4f5993">
<li local-id=3D"acbe5e3f7bde">
<p local-id=3D"811632e63a52">In case that there is a venv still active, ple=
ase run =E2=80=9Cdeactivate=E2=80=9D first</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"13a2571307bc" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.2Tools">6.2&nb=
sp; Tools</h2>
<p local-id=3D"1cf3e7e07f6f">Required tools/extensions for Visual Studio Co=
de:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4f158ec17c42">
<li local-id=3D"42042100b6e8">
<p local-id=3D"2daa0cda8f2a"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://mar=
ketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=3Dms-python.python" rel=3D"nofollo=
w">Python</a></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"389b8c20bb42">
<p local-id=3D"2c1e6f45366e"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://mar=
ketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=3Dms-python.vscode-pylance" rel=3D=
"nofollow">Pylance</a></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c40075c4c74c">
<p local-id=3D"fe008c7543b4"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://mar=
ketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=3Dms-python.black-formatter" rel=
