<h2 local-id=3D"5aa697712268" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.3Tips&amp;tric=
ks">6.3&nbsp; Tips &amp; tricks</h2>
<p local-id=3D"9882ad7559c9">Python is a very strong yet flexible language.=
 Things that are not allowed in other programming languages are allowed in =
Python. Python assumes that the user is mature enough to make their own dec=
isions. This comes with drawbacks.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e6f729d93dc6" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.3.1(Im)mutabil=
ity">6.3.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; (Im)mutability</h3>
<p local-id=3D"f86933bf081f">Programming languages make a difference betwee=
n mutable and immutable:</p>
<p local-id=3D"7e1ac5e71745"><strong>Mutable:</strong><br>
Imagine a box. In that box, you put in a few items of value, gold artifacts=
 etc. I can have the same box but also switch out some of the artifacts. Th=
e box is a mutable item. This also works on the level of computer memory: I=
 can change the contents of a list and switch out the items, but it is stil=
l the same list as before.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a38bd235db04">Mutable items in Python:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7ea462a26886">
<li local-id=3D"f77d287f2d89">
<p local-id=3D"1bcbfa222841">Lists</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"71bd43a04bd8">
<p local-id=3D"34ce71790920">Dicts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4b4ac7072471">
<p local-id=3D"655e3e7af2a7">Sets</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"41a6a74e7e7e">Drawback in this case is as follows:</p>
<p local-id=3D"44495b3217e4">Even though I did not return the dictionary, t=
he contents are still different than the one defined before the function. T=
his is because the memory entry (items in the box) has been changed, but no=
t the memory position (the box itself), meaning dict_to_edit and the value =
that is being edited inside the function are the exact same thing. This lea=
ds to another issue:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a0c8271178e">Since we declare the default value as an initi=
alized dictionary, it means that any changes will only change the memory en=
try and not its position. It will NOT be a fresh dictionary. Also, note tha=
t my linter even complained!</p>
<p local-id=3D"52e53f45d5b2"><strong>Immutable:</strong><br>
Returning to the box example. The items in the box are precious artifacts, =
no other version of it exists. If I were to grab one of those artifacts and=
 I want to change it without losing the original artifact. It means I must =
recreate the original and change whatever I want. The artifact is immutable=
; I cannot change it. If I were to assign a string or a number to a variabl=
e, I cannot change that variable unless I create a new one. Doing 1 + 1 wil=
l not change number 1 into number 2, that would break the entire program, m=
aybe even your computer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d1155f523455">Immutable items:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"97ad76ed2bf5">
<li local-id=3D"19fded5f5d6c">
<p local-id=3D"49e59765cd18">Strings</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2fea3f7bb7ec">
<p local-id=3D"63e1f2acee48">Integers</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0d16d715b5df">
<p local-id=3D"109a906c1510">Tuples</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6304a2b892d9">
<p local-id=3D"02a8c1249e06">Etc</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"3bd5f9df3773" id=3D"OstricaCodingStandards-6.3.2BigO">6.3.2=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Big O</h3>
<p local-id=3D"778a00767d7e">As a developer, you will always run into issue=
s with efficiency and speed. For this you can use the <a class=3D"external-=
link" href=3D"https://wiki.python.org/moin/TimeComplexity" rel=3D"nofollow"=
>Big O notation</a>. There will always be moments that you are developing s=
omething and think it is probably the easiest option to just double-loop th=
rough your data. There is a good reason why this is a bad idea.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b385743fa40f"><strong>Time complexity:</strong><br>
When you loop through a list of 100.000 items, it means that it takes at le=
ast O(n) of time. Whenever I loop through that exact same list inside the s=
ame loop, it turns into a time complexity of O(n^2) because for each list, =
I must go through another 100.000 items. If my loop took 10 minutes to fini=
sh initially, it would now finish in 100 minutes theoretically.</p>
<p local-id=3D"455a5735eb7b">The URL linked above can help you figure out w=
hich datatypes you can use to improve the speeds of your code and the amoun=
t of memory all your variables would use. This will lean more into algorith=
mic work.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9730bd0dd31a">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"bdc9b64bf6bb">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"7f3dfda0efea">&nbsp;</p>
